* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim (issue #27, Part of #16)
* Charge-pump DC characterisation: output current vs. output voltage
* (compliance sweep) at a fixed cascode-mirror reference current (the trim
* code), PVT corner, supply and UP/DN switch state.
*
* `../testbench/run.sh` substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib section:
* mos_tt/mos_ss/mos_ff/mos_sf/mos_fs), @TEMP@ (degC), @VDD@ (supply, V),
* @IREF@ (mirror reference current, A) and @UPV@/@DNV@ (the two switch-input
* voltages, each 0 or @VDD@) per ../corners/matrix.md.
*
* Includes `cp_snap.spice`, a verbatim copy of the frozen
* ../netlist-snapshots/cp.spice (no edit, no strip -- unlike the
* sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table record, this DUT needs no netlist derivation).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TESTBENCH-LOCAL BIAS REPLICA -- NOT PART OF THE COMMITTED DESIGN
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* `cp.sch` exposes its two current legs' tail/cascode gates as four external
* pins (IBP/ICP, IBN/ICN) and contains NO bias generator of its own
* (design/README.md, "Charge pump ... single fixed-current leg per polarity,
* no 2-bit unit-element Icp trim"). Driving those pins with fixed *voltages*
* would make the measured Icp a strong function of process/temperature, which
* is a property of the (absent) bias network, not of the charge pump.
*
* This testbench therefore biases the block the way a cascode current mirror
* is normally biased: a diode-connected replica stack built from devices of
* exactly the same W/L as the leg it mirrors (24u/1u PMOS, 8u/1u NMOS, both
* l=1u -- read off the frozen snapshot, not assumed), driven by an ideal
* reference current @IREF@. The trim code is then @IREF@ itself, and the
* measured Icp is the mirror's own copy of it. The replica devices are
* explicitly labelled XMREF* below so no reader mistakes them for design
* content; ../records/RECORD-001 states the same boundary, and records the
* missing on-chip bias generator as a real design gap rather than papering
* over it.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include cp_snap.spice

Vdd VDD 0 dc @VDD@

* --- P-side cascode mirror reference (testbench-local, see header) ---
XMREFP1 nrp1 nbp  VDD  VDD sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFP2 nbp  nbp  nrp1 VDD sg13_hv_pmos w=24u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefp nbp 0 dc @IREF@

* --- N-side cascode mirror reference (testbench-local, see header) ---
XMREFN1 nrn1 nbn  0    0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMREFN2 nbn  nbn  nrn1 0 sg13_hv_nmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Irefn 0 nbn dc @IREF@

* --- DUT: the real, unmodified cp subckt ---
* .subckt cp UP DN IBP ICP IBN ICN VOUT VDD VSS
XCP up dn nbp nbp nbn nbn vout VDD 0 cp

Vup up 0 dc @UPV@
Vdn dn 0 dc @DNV@
Vout vout 0 dc 1.65

* Compliance sweep: 0.15 V to (VDD - 0.15 V) in 50 mV steps. `icp` below is
* the current the charge pump DELIVERS INTO the vout node (positive = the
* pump SOURCES current into the filter, negative = it SINKS current out of
* it). ngspice's own sign convention for a voltage source's branch current
* -- positive flowing in at the `+` terminal and out through the source --
* makes that exactly `i(Vout)`, with no flip; verified empirically against
* the UP=1/DN=0 case, which must and does come out positive (see
* ../records/RECORD-001 "Sign convention").
.control
dc Vout 0.15 @VOUTMAX@ 0.05
let icp = i(Vout)
wrdata sweep.dat icp
.endc
.end
